## Final Judgement
The evidence confirms that Donald Trump paid exactly $750 in federal income taxes in 2016 and 2017, as reported by the New York Times and corroborated by multiple sources. It also shows that the vast majority of American taxpayers pay more than $750 in federal income taxes annually, with about 90% of middle-income households paying more. The claim’s reference to Trump saying “Because I’m smart. I know how to game the system” is not directly quoted in the evidence, but a similar statement (“That makes me smart”) was made by Trump in a 2016 debate when questioned about his tax returns. The core factual assertion—that Trump paid $750 and that most people pay more—is well-supported, and the quote is a reasonable paraphrase of his known remarks. No evidence contradicts the claim, and it does not omit important context that would change its meaning.

